{"title":"Bisect","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>To <b>bisect</b> a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line_segment\" title=\"Line segment\">line segment</a> is to cut it into two equal parts.  Similarly, to bisect an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angle</a> is to cut it into two equal angles. \n</p><p>See also <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a>.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Bisect&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018074728\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.012 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 7/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 259/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.688      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.688      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4091:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018074728 and revision id 285491. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}